<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dietrich von Fürstenberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1546–1618</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dietrich von Fürstenberg was prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paderborn">Paderborn</a> from 1585 to 1618. A leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/counter-reformation">Counter-Reformation</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a>, he suppressed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> in the city of Paderborn, which he brought to submission in 1604, and restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> across the prince-bishopric. He brought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a> and in 1614 founded the University of Paderborn, the oldest university in Westphalia.</p></div>
